ually carry out maintenance tasks such as managing files and displaying information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="49645">application programming interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371375">АПИ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1124_49645_441548"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of routines that an application uses to request and carry out lower-level services performed by a computer's or device's operating system. These routines usually carry out maintenance tasks such as managing files and displaying information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="49645">application programming interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441548">интерфејс за програмирање апликации</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_1998713_441792"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1998713">non-printable character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441792">непечатлив знак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_85464_441792"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85464">nonprinting character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441792">непечатлив знак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11245_59333_1371684"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A sequence of shades ranging from black through white, used in computer graphics to add detail to images or to represent a color image on a monochrome output device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="59333">grayscale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371684">сиво</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adverb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11246_24169_441329"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To scan a database, a list of files, or the Internet, either for a particular item or for anything that seems to be of interest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="24169">browse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441329">прегледај</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11246_385260_441329"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To scan a database, a list of files, or the Internet, either for a particular item or for anything that seems to be of interest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="385260">browse for</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441329">прегледај</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_1166159_441652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166159">infrared light</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441652">инфрацрвен</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_66343_441652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66343">infrared</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441652">инфрацрвен</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_66344_441652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66344">IR</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441652">инфрацрвен</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11251_209886_442339"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Someone who visits a Web site and purposefully supplies personal information, such as name, address, and phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="209886">registered user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442339">регистриран корисник</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11257_211083_1465439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables records managers to create and manage entries to a “Holds list” such that any document, image, or webpage on that list cannot be deleted, modified, or allowed to expire until the item is removed from the list. The feature is typically used for items that are subject to events such as litigation, audits, or investigations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="211083">Hold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1465439">Држење</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11264_233734_1868198"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of files that can be delivered as a unit to a client computer or device for installation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233734">deployment package</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><t