="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943063">управувачки уредник</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7864_342527_443054"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A logical connection created between two hosts to exchange data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="342527">session</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443054">сесија</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7869_78635_441749"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The key used by the client and server for all session key generation. The master key is used to generate the client-read key, the client-write key, the server-read key, and the server-write key. Master keys can be exported as simple key BLOBs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="78635">master key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441749">главен клуч</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7870_232418_1868176"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A search folder created in Outlook that provides a view of all email items matching specific search criteria and where the items are still stored in one or more Outlook folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232418">Search Folders</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1868176">Папки за пребарување</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7041_441214"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7041">access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441214">пристапен код</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7041_441215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7041">access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441215">лозинка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7042_441214"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7042">password</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441214">пристапен код</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7042_441215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7042">password</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441215">лозинка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7875_307417_2305440"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows Outlook and mobile devices to 