aching, for improved operating-system performance. The IBM OS/2 operating system supports HPFS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61676">high-performance file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1867983">HPFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8983_61677_1867983"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-disk file system that organizes the disk into volumes, rather than partitions and logical drives. HPFS supports long, mixed-case filenames and extended attributes, and implements several levels of caching, for improved operating-system performance. The IBM OS/2 operating system supports HPFS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61677">HPFS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1867983">HPFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9001_1058104_1943125"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A disk directory in which an SMTP service can deposit incoming mail messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1058104">e-mail drop folder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943125">папка за спуштање</term><