hanced views to find and preview digital assets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1512541">asset library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943442">библиотека со средства</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9007_494918_1943442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A library that provides content types with common properties and enhanced views to find and preview digital assets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="494918">Asset Library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943442">библиотека со средства</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9010_347945_443099"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group in the data source that can occur more than once. Controls such as repeating sections and repeating tables are bound to repeating groups.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="347945">repeating group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443099">повторлива група</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9024_1177163_1943033"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In operating systems and database applications, a situation in which two or more processes cannot continue because each process is waiting for resources to be freed by the continuation of the other process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1177163">deadly embrace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943033">застој</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9024_43620_1943033"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In operating systems and database applications, a situation in which two or more processes cannot continue because each process is waiting for resources to be freed by the continuation of the other process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="43620">deadlock</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1943033">застој</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9025_253693_1953721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type that stores a signed, exact numeric value described as the number of digits appearing before and after the decimal point, with a maximum of 29 total digits. All possible digits cannot be represented if you are using the maximum number of digits.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253693">Decimal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1953721">Децимала</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9026_44196_441486"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of rewriting parts of a file to contiguous sectors on a hard disk to increase the speed of access and retrieval.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44196">defragmentation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441486">дефрагментација</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9028_143088_442149"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The blank area between two or more columns of text or between two facing pages in a publication.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143088">gutter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442149">белина за подврзување</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9030_146463_1868094"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a 2-D chart, the area bounded by the axes, including all data series. In a 3-D chart, the area bounded by the axes, including the data series, category names, tick-mark labels, and axis titles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146463">plot area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1868094">област за цртање</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9035_13104_441259"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small piece of code that can be transported over the Internet and executed on the recipient's machine. The term is especially used to refer to such programs as they are embedded in line as objects in HTML documents on the World Wide Web.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="13104">applet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441259">мала апликација</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9040_2624999_2631056"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that allows users to visualize, navigate, and customize the view of files with an XPS document format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2624999">Windows XPS Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2631056">Windows XPS-прикажувач</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9040_386690_2631056"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that allows users to visualize, navigate, and customize the view of files with an XPS document format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="386690">XML Paper Specification Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2631056">Windows XPS-прикажувач</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9040_386691_2631056"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that allows users to visualize, navigate, and customize the view of files with an XPS document format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="386691">XPS Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2631056">Windows XPS-прикажувач</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9064_232419_1868177"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The alternate calendar that is selected from within Outlook. The secondary calendar appears when dual calendar support is enabled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232419">secondary calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1868177">секундарен календар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9067_3665_441192"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software package that replaces an existing version of a product or a feature with a newer and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of the same product or feature. The upgrade process typically leaves existing customer data and preferences intact while replacing the existing software with the newer version.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3665">upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441192">софтверска надградба</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9067_3666_441192"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software package that replaces an existing version of a product or a feature with a newer and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of the same product or feature. The upgrade process typically leaves existing customer data and preferences intact while replacing the existing software with the newer version.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3666">software upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441192">софтверска надградба</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9073_144243_442157"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The condition of a field, record, recordset, or database that makes it read-only to all users except the user currently modifying it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144243">locked</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442157">заклучен</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9074_118405_441971"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The rules governing the formation of a command-line statement, including the order in which a command must be typed, and the elements that follow the command.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="118405">syntax</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441971">синтакса</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9078_144450_442158"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query (SQL statement) that creates a new table and then creates records (rows) in it by copying records from an existing table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144450">make-table query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442158">прашалник за креирање табели</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9078_144450_443138"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query (SQL statement) that creates a new table and then creates records (rows) in it by copying records from an existing table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144450">make-table query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443138">Прашалник за креирање табели</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9078_360105_442158"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query (SQL statement) that creates a new table and then creates records (rows) in it by copying records from an existing table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360105">Make Table query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442158">прашалник за креирање табели</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9078_360105_443138"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query (SQL statement) that creates a new table and then creates records (rows) in it by copying records from an existing table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360105">Make Table query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443138">Прашалник за креирање табели</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9084_152809_442219"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information such as audio, video, images, or text that is contained in a digital media file or stream.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152809">content</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442219">содржина</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9091_358353_2305463"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable users to access their Exchange mailboxes through the application Outlook Web Access and the protocols Exchange ActiveSync, Post Office Protocol version 3 (POP3), and Internet Message Access Protocol 4rev1 (IMAP4). The Client Access server role also includes Web services that are used by other Exchange 2007 server roles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358353">Client Access server role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2305463">улога на сервер за пристап на клиенти</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="910_748601_1372289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of email addresses that is treated as a single recipient for email distribution purposes, and that is created by and available to an individual Outlook user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748601">contact group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1372289">група за контакт</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9101_140120_442121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A window that you can display when a data access page is open in Design view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="