by using Internet Protocol security (IPsec).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262694">Internet Key Exchange</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442616">Internet Key Exchange</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9583_262695_1371634"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A protocol that establishes the security association and shared keys necessary for computers to communicate by using Internet Protocol security (IPsec).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262695">IKE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371634">ИКЕ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9583_262695_442616"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A protocol that establishes the security association and shared keys necessary for computers to communicate by using Internet Protocol security (IPsec).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262695">IKE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442616">Internet Key Exchange</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9590_134813_442071"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To prevent the writing (recording) of information, usually on a disk.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="134813">write-protect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442071">заштита од запишување</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9596_340142_1832423"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The option that causes the device to vibrate instead of playing an audible notification or alert tone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="340142">Vibrate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1832423">вибрации</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9597_347918_443093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A filter effect in Windows Movie Maker.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="347918">Grayscale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="443093">Сиво</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9605_117359_3075023"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To start using the services of a service provider, e.g. an Internet access provider.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="117359">subscribe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3075023">претплатете се</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9608_183935_1465432"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic element on a drawing that is associated with data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="183935">data graphic</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1465432">податочна графика</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9610_2296363_1371635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of authentication methods (NTLM, Kerberos, and Negotiate) used to provide transport-level security.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296363">Integrated Windows Authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371635">НТЛМ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9610_2296364_1371635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of authentication methods (NTLM, Kerberos, and Negotiate) used to provide transport-level security.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296364">IWA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371635">НТЛМ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9610_262690_1371635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of authentication methods (NTLM, Kerberos, and Negotiate) used to provide transport-level security.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262690">NTLM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371635">НТЛМ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9610_2834199_1371635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of authentication methods (NTLM, Kerberos, and Negotiate) used to provide transport-level security.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834199">Windows authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1371635">НТЛМ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9612_318139_442887"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of four fields of an SCODE that indicates the system service responsible for the error. It consists of a unique number that is assigned to represent the error or warning.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318139">facility field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442887">поле за пријава на грешка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="963_232834_1372290"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The first row in a spreadsheet. The header row contains category labels that describe the contents of the columns.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232834">header row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1372290">насловен ред</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9638_210467_1096002"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role name of a server that services queries in the farm topology.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210467">query role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1096002">улога на прашалник</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9648_233439_2305678"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An audio message played over the telephone to explain valid options to users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233439">prompt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2305678">потсетник</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="965_317875_442873"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To display the subentries contained within a folder or outline view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="317875">expand</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442873">прошири</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9651_138544_1868039"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual cue to indicate which formatting will be applied when you double-click: a left-aligned, centered, or right-aligned tab stop; a left indent; or left or right text wrapping.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="138544">Click and Type pointer shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1868039">Форма на покажувач за кликнување и пишување</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9654_315160_442852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Of, pertaining to, or characteristic of an electronic circuit or hardware grouping in which the configuration is determined by the physical interconnection of the components (as opposed to being programmable in software or alterable by a switch).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="315160">wired</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="442852">физички поврзан</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">MKD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9660_308305_442790"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A stored version 